      "content": "it's just constant noise in my head. i keep thinking about how easy it would be to just stop. everyone would finally stop looking at me with those pitying eyes, and i wouldn't have to deal with the shame of having to explain why i'm a complete waste of space. if the version of me that mattered is gone, then what's the point of all this heavy lifting? it feels like i'm just dragging around a corpse. i don't want to \"reconstruct\" anything. i just want the feeling that everything is broken to stop. doesn't it seem more logical to just let it go?",
